  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "Transaction **TX-0401** is in your records and the amount is verified:\n\n- **Amount:** 240.00 EUR\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** outgoing card payment, status settled\n\nI also see **TX-0402**, which is also 240.00 EUR to TechMart Online, dated 2026-07-14 and settled. I'm noting it only as a factual match. I haven't checked whether it relates to your concern.\n\nThese reason codes can be used for disputes. Which one fits depends on what happened:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 could be relevant here.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** A card payment was made without your authorization and the card was not physically present, such as an online payment you did not make.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** Money was taken from your account without your permission.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid for something that was never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nPlease tell me what happened with TX-0401. I can then check whether a dispute under the relevant code is eligible before anything is filed. I won't open a dispute without your confirmation.",
